================================================================================
py4DSTEM
================================================================================

mac4DSTEM implements 4D-STEM analysis algorithms ported from py4DSTEM, which is
used as the reference implementation and validated against.

    py4DSTEM — https://github.com/py4dstem/py4DSTEM
    Copyright (C) the py4DSTEM developers
    Licensed under the GNU General Public License v3.0

Because substantial parts of this work are derived from py4DSTEM, mac4DSTEM is
licensed under the GPL v3.0 as well. Ported routines carry an inline `DEVIATION`
note in the source wherever this implementation departs from py4DSTEM, together
with the reason and a reference to the corresponding py4DSTEM source location.

If you use mac4DSTEM for published work, please cite py4DSTEM as the origin of
the underlying methods:

    Savitzky, B. H. et al. "py4DSTEM: A Software Package for Four-Dimensional
    Scanning Transmission Electron Microscopy Data Analysis."
    Microscopy and Microanalysis 27, 712–743 (2021).


================================================================================
eXSpy and HyperSpy (EDX spectroscopy)
================================================================================

The X-ray line table (`mac4DSTEM/Core/Spectroscopy/XRayLineData.swift`: line
energies from Chantler 2005, relative line weights from the EPQ library, both as
eXSpy ships them), the detector line-width law, and the integration and
background window rules are ported from eXSpy, with HyperSpy's channel rounding
and slicing. They are validated against it, and carry inline `DEVIATION` notes
where this implementation departs.

    eXSpy — https://github.com/hyperspy/exspy, commit 7185a4d1
    Copyright (C) 2007-2026 The eXSpy developers
    HyperSpy — https://github.com/hyperspy/hyperspy, version 2.4.0
    Copyright (C) The HyperSpy developers
    Both licensed under the GNU General Public License v3.0 or later

